<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 162 0 R
/T (Hardware Village brings together hands-on hardware hacking and wireless security in one interactive space, giving attendees a practical look at how everyday devices communicate and where their security can fail. Participants will explore real consumer and IoT devices through live, non-malicious demonstrations that highlight firmware analysis, hardware interfaces, and wireless vulnerabilities. A dedicated radio security component introduces the fundamentals of the radio spectrum, signal capture, and replay attacks, showing how signals from devices like routers, key fobs, and NFC systems can be analyzed by defenders. Designed for both beginners and advanced learners, this village offers a rare opportunity to see how hardware, firmware, and radio security intersect in real-world systems.)
/E (Hardware Village brings together hands-on hardware hacking and wireless security in one interactive space, giving attendees a practical look at how everyday devices communicate and where their security can fail. Participants will explore real consumer and IoT devices through live, non-malicious demonstrations that highlight firmware analysis, hardware interfaces, and wireless vulnerabilities. A dedicated radio security component introduces the fundamentals of the radio spectrum, signal capture, and replay attacks, showing how signals from devices like routers, key fobs, and NFC systems can be analyzed by defenders. Designed for both beginners and advanced learners, this village offers a rare opportunity to see how hardware, firmware, and radio security intersect in real-world systems.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
